  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>e3a0545544fcca4f1efc7c172ced4dd5</srcmd5>
    <version>2.11.2</version>
    <time>1787849495</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-pydantic-extra-types to 2.11.2.

Upstream changes:
- TimeZoneName validator accepts common timezone abbreviations such as EDT
- Negative pendulum Duration values now serialize to correct ISO 8601
- Missing Pendulum Interval wrapper support added
- New ISIN type with checksum validation
- New JsonSchema type validated through jsonschema

A note on the version, since PyPI reports 2.11.1 as latest: upstream yanked
2.11.2 from PyPI because the two new types (ISIN, JsonSchema) were merged into
what was meant to be a patch release. The yank reason states there are no known
security risks, both types are kept on upstream master, and no successor release
has appeared in the four months since. Fedora, Gentoo, Arch and FreeBSD all ship
2.11.2. The three genuine bugfixes above only exist in this release.

Packaging changes:
- Add fix-tests-for-pydantic-2.13.patch, the upstream merge commit from
  gh#pydantic/pydantic-extra-types#394, needed because pydantic 2.13 adds a
  description member to the Coordinate JSON schema that the tests did not expect
- Replace the previous import smoke test with the real upstream test suite;
  13497 tests pass per Python flavour. tests/test_cron.py, tests/test_ulid.py
  and tests/test_json_schema.py stay excluded because cron-converter and
  python-ulid are not packaged in Factory
- jsonschema is a new test-only dependency (python-jsonschema 4.26.0 is in
  Factory); it is an optional extra upstream, so it is not a runtime Requires

Built natively on aarch64: rpmlint 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1373870</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
